 8 km per source pixel near the disk center; detail becomes coarser toward the edge. This is display color, not calibrated I/F or albedo. Only views within 65° of the surface normal are retained; gray grid marks the rest of the globe. Photographed shading and color fringes remain; added globe lighting is approximate.","summary":"May 2001 Galileo color over about 29% of the globe. Gray grid: unseen or withheld. Processed display colors, not albedo.","facts":[{"id":"release","label":"Observation","value":"Galileo · May 2001"},{"id":"coverage","label":"Retained footprint","value":"28.74% of the globe · emission ≤65°"},{"id":"resolution","label":"Source detail","value":"About 8 km per pixel near the disk center"}],"legend":{"kind":"categories","title":"Coverage","items":[{"label":"Color","description":"Variable published RGB across observed terrain; this swatch is only a visual key.","color":"rgb(142 100 80)"},{"label":"Gray grid","description":"Unseen or withheld surface; no reconstructed colors.","color":"rgb(119 119 119)"}]},"legendNote":"Photographic colors have no numeric scale; they are the publisher’s processed display colors.","title":"Processed color mosaic"},{"id":"infrared","label":"Infrared","detail":"NIMS spectral bands","thumbnailUrl":"/scenes/callisto/callisto-lens-infrared.webp","description":"Galileo NIMS observations assign red, green and blue to 0.77, 2.25 and 3.66 µm, following the archive guide. This false-color view shows spectral differences, not natural color or mineral abundance. The observations have Minnaert photometric correction; resolution, residual brightness and seams vary. Fixed channel stretches clip extreme values. Gray grid marks areas lacking a valid sample in any selected band.","title":"Galileo NIMS spectral color"}]},"settings":{"title":{"label":"Settings","src":"/shell/title-settings.svg","width":65.55,"height":23,"source":"Inter Variable 4.001 git-9221beed3","sourceUrl":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rsms/inter/9221beed3/doc